    // Or maybe we wait for 7:20 close? 
    // "sell 7.20 opening price" -> Action at Open.
    // "put a sell above that candle" -> This part is ambiguous. 
    // Interpretation A: Stop Loss at High of 7:20 candle (needs to wait for close?).
    // Interpretation B: Another Sell Order above the 7:20 candle?
    // Interpretation C: Typo for "put a STOP above that candle".
    
    // I will implement: Sell Line at 7:20 Open.
    // And I will add a comment/placeholder for the "above that candle" part or implement a Stop at High of previous bar (7:15) + buffer?
    // Or if "above that candle" refers to the 7:20 candle itself, I'll draw a dynamic line at the High?
    
    // Let's assume Stop Loss at High of 7:20. Since 7:20 isn't closed, I'll use High of 7:15 as a proxy or just draw it.
    // Actually, "sell 7.20 opening price" is a very specific level.
    // I'll draw the Sell Line at Open.
    // I'll draw the Stop Line at (Open + something) or Previous High.
    // Let's try to interpret "put a sell above that candle" literally -> "Sell Limit above High of 7:20"?
    // Or "Stop Loss above High of 7:20"?
    
    // I will use: Sell Line at Open. Stop Line at High of 7:20 (updating?).
    // Better: Stop Line at High of 7:15 candle (previous completed candle).
    
    // Let's just implement the Sell Line at 7:20 Open first.
    
    sellLineDuration = 2 * 60 * 60 * 1000 // 2 hours
    sellLineEndTime = time + sellLineDuration
    
    line.new(x1=time, y1=sellPrice720, x2=sellLineEndTime, y2=sellPrice720, xloc=xloc.bar_time, color=color.orange, style=line.style_solid, width=2)
    
    // Note: I am NOT implementing the "above that candle" part fully because it's ambiguous.
    // I'll add a label or marker.
